# Development

Initialize with `go mod init {{project_slug}}`, then resolve the modules, add
templ's CLI as a tool and fetch htmx:

```sh
go get github.com/a-h/templ github.com/stretchr/testify github.com/PuerkitoBio/goquery
go get -tool github.com/a-h/templ/cmd/templ
make htmx
make generate
go mod tidy
make install
```

`go tool templ` runs the CLI at the version go.mod records, the same version as
the runtime library, so generated code always matches it. Upgrade both with
`go get -tool github.com/a-h/templ/cmd/templ@latest`, then `make generate`.

`make htmx` reads the newest release from npm's `latest` tag and downloads its
`htmx.min.js`; `HTMX_VERSION=<version> make htmx` fetches a specific one.
Commit the file and record its version in AGENTS.md. The binary embeds it, so
the build fails until it exists.

If the project chooses a remote module path, change it with `go mod edit
-module <path>` and replace `{{project_slug}}/` imports in every Go file.
Install golangci-lint using its official instructions, and write its installed
version to `.golangci-lint-version`.

```sh
make generate-check templ-fmt-check htmx-check fmt-check vet lint build test test-integration
go test -race -run TestHTMXPostWithErrorsRetargetsTheForm ./internal/web/
make coverage
```

After editing a `.templ` file, run `make generate` (the Claude hook does it on
save) and commit the `.templ` and `_templ.go` files together. `make fmt`
formats `.templ` files with `templ fmt` and hand-written Go with gofmt and
goimports; it never touches `_templ.go`.

Component tests render a component into a buffer and query it with goquery.
Handler tests run the real handler under `httptest.NewServer` with redirects
disabled and assert status, `HX-*` headers and the HTML. Tagged integration
tests build the server once in TestMain, start it on PORT=0, read its address
from the JSON logs and stop it with SIGINT and SIGTERM. Everything runs with
the race detector, which needs cgo and a C compiler.

Fill README and the selected fragments' AGENTS, hook and CI guidance before
the final `stacks verify`. The default hooks and workflow are supplied by
their fragments; this slice does not write their files.
